education_match_percent":62,"resume_score":58,"summary":"[SYNTHETIC DEMO] Retail sales associate exploring a first B2B account executive position. Sales Associate | Pine Meadow Retail (fictional) | 2023-2026 Assisted customers, met daily service targets, and processed purchases. No B2B quota ownership claimed. Customer Service Associate | Oak Lane Market (fictional) | 2021-2023 Resolved routine returns and maintained accurate transaction records. Follow-up: Use a practical discovery exercise and assess whether a junior sales pathway is more appropriate."},"resume_url":"sales-demo/d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000001003.pdf","resume_original_filename":"taylor-reed-synthetic-resume.pdf","resume_mime_type":"application/pdf","resume_parse_status":"parsed","phone":null,"phone_e164":null},{"id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000002001","client_id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000000001","role_id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000000200","name":"Casey Bennett","first_name":"Casey","last_name":"Bennett","email":"casey.bennett@example.invalid","status":"review_ready","interview_status":"completed","created_at":"2026-10-06T21:00:00.000Z","upload_ts":"2026-10-06T21:00:00.000Z","candidate_id":"SYNTHETIC-2001","analysis_summary":{"experience_match_percent":92,"skills_match_percent":93,"education_match_percent":82,"resume_score":90,"summary":"[SYNTHETIC DEMO] Support specialist with four years of structured help-desk experience. Support Specialist | Harbor Path Systems (fictional) | 2022-2026 Handled 35-45 cases daily using a ticketing system, documented reproducible defects, and coached new support staff. Customer Service Associate | Spruce Point Services (fictional) | 2020-2022 Managed scheduling questions and routine account inquiries. Follow-up: Validate case-quality examples and discuss adapting the process to staffing-client workflows."},"resume_url":"sales-demo/d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000002001.pdf","resume_original_filename":"casey-bennett-synthetic-resume.pdf","resume_mime_type":"application/pdf","resume_parse_status":"parsed","phone":null,"phone_e164":null},{"id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000002002","client_id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000000001","role_id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000000200","name":"Riley Chen","first_name":"Riley","last_name":"Chen","email":"riley.chen@example.invalid","status":"review_ready","interview_status":"completed","created_at":"2026-10-06T21:00:00.000Z","upload_ts":"2026-10-06T21:00:00.000Z","candidate_id":"SYNTHETIC-2002","analysis_summary":{"experience_match_percent":74,"skills_match_percent":79,"education_match_percent":72,"resume_score":75,"summary":"[SYNTHETIC DEMO] Customer service professional developing technical support and escalation skills. Customer Service Representative | Willow Bridge Commerce (fictional) | 2023-2026 Handled order questions and account changes. Used standard templates and escalated technical cases to a lead. Service Desk Intern | Meadowbrook Services (fictional) | 2022-2023 Categorized inbound tickets and assisted with customer follow-ups. Follow-up: Use a triage exercise to test business-impact prioritization and privacy-safe escalation notes."},"resume_url":"sales-demo/d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000002002.pdf","resume_original_filename":"riley-chen-synthetic-resume.pdf","resume_mime_type":"application/pdf","resume_parse_status":"parsed","phone":null,"phone_e164":null},{"id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000002003","client_id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000000001","role_id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000000200","name":"Morgan Blake","first_name":"Morgan","last_name":"Blake","email":"morgan.blake@example.invalid","status":"review_ready","interview_status":"completed","created_at":"2026-10-06T21:00:00.000Z","upload_ts":"2026-10-06T21:00:00.000Z","candidate_id":"SYNTHETIC-2003","analysis_summary":{"experience_match_percent":52,"skills_match_percent":60,"education_match_percent":63,"resume_score":57,"summary":"[SYNTHETIC DEMO] Administrative assistant seeking a first dedicated support role. Administrative Assistant | Elm Crest Studio (fictional) | 2023-2026 Scheduled appointments, answered general inquiries, and maintained office records. Reception Volunteer | Fictional Community Workshop | 2022-2023 Directed visitors and passed requests to staff. Follow-up: Assess a coached troubleshooting scenario and train on verification, triage, and case-note standards."},"resume_url":"sales-demo/d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000002003.pdf","resume_original_filename":"morgan-blake-synthetic-resume.pdf","resume_mime_type":"application/pdf","resume_parse_status":"parsed","phone":null,"phone_e164":null}],"interviews":[{"id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000011001","candidate_id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000001001","client_id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000000001","role_id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000000100","transcript":"[SYNTHETIC DEMO TRANSCRIPT - no real interview was conducted]\n\nQ1 - Interviewer: Describe a discovery call that changed your sales approach. What did you learn and what did you do?\nAvery Morgan: A regional client asked for twenty placements in four weeks. I asked about coverage gaps, attrition, and manager availability. The real constraint was weekend coverage, not headcount. I mapped the five critical shifts and brought delivery into a scoping call. We proposed eight initial placements with weekly checkpoints instead of promising twenty. The first cohort covered all five shifts and the client expanded after six weeks.\n\nQ2 - Interviewer: How do you manage your pipeline and forecast? Give a concrete example.\nAvery Morgan: Every Friday I inspect stage age, a dated next step, the decision process, and a customer-confirmed timeline. In Q3 I removed two verbal commitments from commit because procurement had not approved terms. That reduced my forecast from $310,000 to $245,000; we closed $238,000. My manager could plan delivery capacity using the smaller, defensible number.\n\nQ3 - Interviewer: Tell me about a price objection and how you handled it without overpromising.\nAvery Morgan: A buyer said our fee was eighteen percent above another offer. I clarified the scope and showed our agreed service levels, not unsupported competitor claims. I offered a smaller pilot at the published rate rather than a discount I could not authorize. The buyer selected the pilot. I documented the assumptions and did not guarantee a hiring outcome.\n\nQ4 - Interviewer: How do you hand a newly won account to the delivery team?\nAvery Morgan: Before handoff I review the signed scope, contacts, success measures, promised timelines, and open risks with delivery. The client joins a kickoff. For one account I highlighted a pending security review and assigned an owner before work began. I stayed through the first checkpoint and confirmed the customer understood the next steps.","status":"completed","is_active":false,"attempt_number":1,"attempt_mode":"video","created_at":"2026-10-07T21:00:00.000Z","started_at":"2026-10-07T21:00:00.000Z","ended_at":"2026-10-07T21:00:00.000Z","has_substantive_response":true,"substantive_response_count":4,"candidate_utterance_count":4,"transcript_available":true,"recording_status":"demo_placeholder","video_url":null,"transcript_scores":{"overall":92,"confidence":94,"ai_aided_risk":"low","ai_aided_risk_reason":"Simulated demo signal for follow-up examples only, not evidence of AI use by a real person.","rubric_scores":[{"category":"Discovery and qualification","weight":30,"score":94,"evidence":"Q1 - Discovery and qualification (94/100; weight 30%): \"A regional client asked for twenty placements in four weeks. I asked about coverage gaps, attrition, and manager availability. The real constraint was weekend coverage, not headcount. I mapped the five critical shifts and brought delivery into a scoping call. We proposed eight initial placements with weekly checkpoints instead of promising twenty. The first cohort covered all five shifts and the client expanded after six weeks.\""},{"catego