A prospect wanted a product demonstration. I asked about team size and their current process, then learned their manager was not involved. I added a manager discovery meeting before the demo. It helped us explain the right workflow, although I did not track the eventual operational result.\n\nQ2 - Interviewer: How do you manage your pipeline and forecast? Give a concrete example.\nJordan Ellis: I review opportunities each Monday and update dates. I use my judgment about how positive the calls feel. Last month two deals moved to the next quarter after purchasing delays. I had included both in commit. I am starting to require a confirmed decision date but cannot give a forecast-accuracy figure yet.\n\nQ3 - Interviewer: Tell me about a price objection and how you handled it without overpromising.\nJordan Ellis: When a customer raised price, I asked what budget they had and reviewed the basic package. My manager approved a smaller scope. I did not promise a discount independently. The customer kept talking with us, but I did not personally own the closing decision.\n\nQ4 - Interviewer: How do you hand a newly won account to the delivery team?\nJordan Ellis: I send an email with the contract and contact names to the account team. I try to attend the kickoff. I do not yet use a standard checklist for risks or customer success measures; our account manager fills those in.","status":"completed","is_active":false,"attempt_number":1,"attempt_mode":"video","created_at":"2026-10-07T21:00:00.000Z","started_at":"2026-10-07T21:00:00.000Z","ended_at":"2026-10-07T21:00:00.000Z","has_substantive_response":true,"substantive_response_count":4,"candidate_utterance_count":4,"transcript_available":true,"recording_status":"demo_placeholder","video_url":null,"transcript_scores":{"overall":74,"confidence":72,"ai_aided_risk":"medium","ai_aided_risk_reason":"Simulated demo signal for follow-up examples only, not evidence of AI use by a real person.","rubric_scores":[{"category":"Discovery and 