ge. My manager approved a smaller scope. I did not promise a discount independently. The customer kept talking with us, but I did not personally own the closing decision.\""},{"category":"Client handoff","weight":20,"score":72,"evidence":"Q4 - Client handoff (72/100; weight 20%): \"I send an email with the contract and contact names to the account team. I try to attend the kickoff. I do not yet use a standard checklist for risks or customer success measures; our account manager fills those in.\""}],"synthetic":true,"clarity":79,"confidence":73,"engagement":81,"evaluation_reliability":72,"ai_aided_risk":"medium","conditions":{"evaluation_conditions":"Adequate","signal_confidence":"Moderate","audio_quality_issues":"Minor","distraction_risk":"Medium"},"integrity_risk":"Medium"},"analysis":{"summary":"[SYNTHETIC DEMO] Mixed evidence. Communicates customer situations clearly, with uneven specificity on forecasting and full-cycle ownership. The simulated presentation shows moderate confidence and good engagement; probe the gaps with a practical example. Probe forecast criteria and ask for a complete, personally owned close-to-delivery example.","evidence":["Q1 - Discovery and qualification (78/100; weight 30%): \"A prospect wanted a product demonstration. I asked about team size and their current process, then learned their manager was not involved. I added a manager discovery meeting before the demo. It helped us explain the right workflow, although I did not track the eventual operational result.\"","Q2 - Pipeline discipline (68/100; weight 25%): \"I review opportunities each Monday and update dates. I use my judgment about how positive the calls feel. Last month two deals moved to the next quarter after purchasing delays. I had included both in commit. I am starting to require a confirmed decision date but cannot give a forecast-accuracy figure yet.\"","Q3 - Objection handling (76/100; weight 25%): \"When a customer raised price, I asked what budget they had and reviewed the basic package. My manager approved a smaller scope. I did not promise a discount independently. The customer kept talking with us, but I did not personally own the closing decision.\"","Q4 - Client handoff (72/100; weight 20%): \"I send an email with the contract and contact names to the account team. I try to attend the kickoff. I do not yet use a standard checklist for risks or customer success measures; our account manager fills those in.\""],"limitations":["Limited direct ownership evidence; no inference about capability outside the specific examples provided.","Synthetic scores are illustrative, not real assessment results.","All communication, audio, distraction, confidence and risk signals are synthetic display examples. No real audio/video was analyzed."]},"unanswered_candidate_questions":["Probe forecast criteria and ask for a complete, personally owned close-to-delivery example."]},{"id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000021003","candidate_id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000001003","client_id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000000001","role_id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000000100","interview_id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000011003","attempt_number":1,"report_kind":"complete_interview","created_at":"2026-10-07T21:00:00.000Z","report_generated_at":"2026-10-07T21:00:00.000Z","resume_score":58,"interview_score":51,"overall_score":55,"resume_breakdown":{"experience_match_percent":50,"skills_match_percent":65,"education_match_percent":62,"resume_score":58,"summary":"[SYNTHETIC DEMO] Retail sales associate exploring a first B2B account executive position. Sales Associate | Pine Meadow Retail (fictional) | 2023-2026 Assisted customers, met daily service targets, and processed purchases. No B2B quota ownership claimed. Customer Service Associate | Oak Lane Market (fictional) | 2021-2023 Resolved routine returns and maintained accurate transaction records. Follow-up: Use a practical discovery exercise and assess whether a junior sales pathway is more appropriate."},"interview_breakdown":{"summary":"[SYNTHETIC DEMO] Limited evidence. Answers remain general and acknowledge limited B2B experience. The simulated presentation is hesitant but cooperative; use a coached discovery exercise before interpreting the missing role-specific evidence. Use a practical discovery exercise and assess whether a junior sales pathway is more appropriate.","rubric_scores":[{"category":"Discovery and qualification","weight":30,"score":52,"evidence":"Q1 - Discovery and qualification (52/100; weight 30%): \"I usually explain the features first and ask whether the price works. In retail I helped someone compare two products. I have not run a business discovery call or mapped decision-makers, so I would need a process and coaching.\""},{"category":"Pipeline discipline","weight":25,"score":48,"evidence":"Q2 - Pipeline discipline (48/100; weight 25%): \"I keep a personal list and contact people when I have time. I have not used a formal opportunity pipeline or forecast model. I would mark a deal likely when a customer seemed interested, but I cannot provide an accuracy example.\""},{"category":"Objection handling","weight":25,"score":54,"evidence":"Q3 - Objection handling (54/100; weight 25%): \"I would tell the customer we are the best and try to get a lower price approved. I do not yet know how to compare staffing service levels. I would ask my manager before making a guarantee or offering a discount.\""},{"category":"Client handoff","weight":20,"score":50,"evidence":"Q4 - Client handoff (50/100; weight 20%): \"I would send the buyer information to the next team. I have not done an account kickoff and cannot give an example of documenting delivery risks. A checklist would help me know what to include.\""}],"synthetic":true,"clarity":61,"confidence":54,"engagement":66,"evaluation_reliability":46,"ai_aided_risk":"high","conditions":{"evaluation_conditions":"Limited","signal_confidence":"Low","audio_quality_issues":"Moderate","distraction_risk":"High"},"integrity_risk":"High"},"analysis":{"summary":"[SYNTHETIC DEMO] Limited evidence. Answers remain general and acknowledge limited B2B experience. The simulated presentation is hesitant but cooperative; use a coached discovery exercise before interpreting the missing role-specific evidence. Use a practical discovery exercise and assess whether a junior sales pathway is more appropriate.","evidence":["Q1 - Discovery and qualification (52/100; weight 30%): \"I usually explain the features first and ask whether the price works. In retail I helped someone compare two products. I have not run a business discovery call or mapped decision-makers, so I would need a process and coaching.\"","Q2 - Pipeline discipline (48/100; weight 25%): \"I keep a personal list and contact people when I have time. I have not used a formal opportunity pipeline or forecast model. I would mark a deal likely when a customer seemed interested, but I cannot provide an accuracy example.\"","Q3 - Objection handling (54/100; weight 25%): \"I would tell the customer we are the best and try to get a lower price approved. I do not yet know how to compare staffing service levels. I would ask my manager before making a guarantee or offering a discount.\"","Q4 - Client handoff (50/100; weight 20%): \"I would send the buyer information to the next team. I have not done an account kickoff and cannot give an example of documenting delivery risks. A checklist would help me know what to include.\""],"limitations":["Limited role-specific experience was explicitly acknowledged. Do not equate a low demo score with a general hiring recommendation.","Synthetic scores are illustrative, not real assessment results.","All communication, audio, distraction, confidence and risk signals are synthetic display examples. No real audio/video was analyzed."]},"unanswered_candidate_questions":["Use a practical discovery exercise and assess whether a junior sales pathway is more appropriate."]},{"id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000022001","candidate_id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000002001","client_id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000000001","role_id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000000200","interview_id":"d38ade00-2026-4000-8000-000000012001","attempt_number":1,"report_kind":"complete_interview","created_at":"2026-10-07T21:00:00.000Z","report_generated_at":"2026-10-07T21:00:00.000Z","resume_score":90,"interview_score":93,"overall_score":92,"resume_breakdown":{"experience_match_percent":92,"skills_match_percent":93,"education_match_percent":82,"resume_score":90,"summary":"[SYNTHETIC DEMO] Support specialist with four years of structured help-desk experience. Support Specialist | Harbor Path Systems (fictional) | 2022-2026 Handled 35-45 cases daily using a ticketing system, documented reproducible defects, and coached new support staff. Customer Service Associate | Spruce Point Services (fictional) | 2020-2022 Managed scheduling questions and routine account inquiries. Follow-up: Validate case-quality examples and discuss adapting the process to staffing-client workflows."},"interview_breakdown":{"summary":"[SYNTHETIC DEMO] Strong evidence. Explains troubleshooting, impact-based triage, and privacy-safe documentation in a clear sequence. The simulated presentation is confident and attentive; validate case-quality examples in follow-up. Validate case-quality examples and discuss adapting the process to staffing-client workflows.","rubric_scores":[{"category":"Customer communication","weight":30,"score":93,"evidence":"Q1 - Customer communication (93/100; weight 30%): \"A customer had lost access before a deadline. I acknowledged the impact, repeated the goal, and gave a twenty-minute update commitment rather than promising an immediate fix. I checked access logs, involved the account administrator, and sent updates until restored. I documented the cause and confirmed they could complete the task.\""},{"category":"Troubleshooting","weight":30,"score":92,"evidence":"Q2 - Troubleshooting (92/100